    feat(bills): CRUD endpoints, expense linking and attachment streaming
    
    Completes the bills feature started by the AI scanner: a scanned extraction
    could be read but never persisted.
    
    POST/GET/PUT/PATCH/DELETE /api/bills, plus /summary and /:id/file, with two
    invariants across every handler:
    
    - Ownership. Every query is scoped by req.user._id, and another user's bill is
      reported as 404 rather than 403, since a 403 would confirm the id exists.
    
    - Exactly one linked Expense. Saving a bill writes the Expense first, then the
      Bill which references it, so no failure path can leave a Bill pointing at a
      row that does not exist. This deliberately avoids multi-document
      transactions, which MongoDB only offers on a replica set.
    
    Attachments are validated by magic bytes at save time as well as at scan time,
    held in GridFS with no public URL, and streamed only to their owner with nosniff
    and no-store headers.
    
    invoiceNumber is normalized to an absent path rather than null, enforced by a
    schema setter so every "no number" spelling - omitted, null, empty or
    whitespace - collapses to the same state. The unique index becomes a partial
    one over documents where the field is actually a string: a sparse index only
    skips a wholly missing field, so a stored null would still be indexed and would
    make every unnumbered bill from a vendor collide with the next.
    
    saveAnyway now requires affirmative consent (true/on/1/yes). An unchecked
    checkbox posts nothing, so an empty string is never a legitimate yes, and
    treating it as one silently disabled duplicate detection for every scanned
    bill. Ambiguous input now fails towards the duplicate check.
    
    The /scan payload is unchanged; the two fixes are in the shared model.
    
    Also drops the leftover Supabase schema.sql, superseded by the MERN migration.
    
    Tests: 130 cases (130/130 passing) across 3 files.

