    Upload safety
    - multer memoryStorage only; auth runs before multer so an unauthenticated
      upload is rejected without buffering a byte
    - type decided by magic bytes, never by extension or the client's Content-Type
      (a PHP webshell named .png is rejected)
    - 8 MB ceiling mapped to 413, multer errors to the standard JSON error shape
    
    Extraction
    - gemini-2.5-flash multimodal, media part before the prompt per Google's
      single-page guidance, responseMimeType + responseSchema so the model is
      constrained to the contract rather than free-text prose
    - prompt forbids inventing values, requires plain unseparated numbers, and
      covers English, Urdu, Roman Urdu and Pakistani formats (Rs./PKR, GST, TDS,
      day-first dates)
    - Zod validation, then a 1% tolerance audit that *reports* sum(items) vs
      subtotal and subtotal+tax-discount vs total instead of quietly correcting
      them
    - suggestedCategory is pinned to a category the user actually owns
    
    Reliability and privacy
    - 10 scans/hour per user, since each call is a paid inference
    - one retry on transport/timeout/5xx/malformed output, then a friendly
      enter-manually fallback; no retry on non-retryable 4xx
    - logs outcome, MIME type and byte count only - never bill contents, never the
      AI response, never the API key
    
    Fixed two bugs the tests exposed
    - coerceIsoDate parsed 05/03/2026 as 5 May, silently transposing day and month
      on exactly the day-first Pakistani format this feature targets; day-first
      numeric dates are now parsed explicitly and 31/02 is rejected as invalid
    - roundMoney and toMinor lost half a paisa on exact .005 values because 1.005
      is stored as 1.00499...; a sub-minor-unit epsilon nudge fixes the rounding
    
