    feat(bills): bill model, atomic invoice counter, GridFS storage, pure calculations
    
    Phase 1 of the Bills & Invoices feature: persistence and the calculation rules
    the rest of the feature is built on.
    
    Bill model
    - stores every monetary value as integer minor units, never floats
    - links exactly one Expense via .expense
    - file { storageKey, mimeType, size, originalName } for the authenticated preview
    - source: scanned | manual; status: paid | unpaid | overdue
    - compound index on (user, issueDate) for statements and lists
    - unique sparse index on (user, vendor, invoiceNumber); invoiceNumber is left
      undefined rather than null so sparse correctly ignores unnumbered manual bills
    
    Status is stored as paid/unpaid only. overdue is derived from dueDate by
    resolveBillStatus() at read time, because a stored status cannot stay correct as
    due dates pass.
    
    Counter model
    - INV-2026-0001 via findOneAndUpdate + \ + upsert, which MongoDB applies
      atomically; the 11000 race loser falls back to a plain increment
    
    billStorageService
    - GridFS by default (single deployment, no second service to secure)
    - optional Cloudinary via BILL_STORAGE=cloudinary, loaded with a dynamic import
      so the optional dependency is not required otherwise
    - attachments stored with type=authenticated; there is no public URL path
    - attacker-controlled filenames are stripped of path and shell metacharacters
    
    utils/billCalculations (pure, unit tested)
    - coerceAmount handles Rs./PKR/separators/parenthesised negatives
    - coerceIsoDate avoids the UTC shift that would move a due date by a day
    - computeTotals is the single source of truth for live recalculation
    - auditBillArithmetic reports 1% tolerance breaches instead of fixing them
    - summarizeBills, pickUpcomingBills, pickDueSoonAlerts for widget and statements

